#~ shadowed_header
# fixedbugs, defect 2333 (panel 237's R5, the compiler-engineer's harmful
# stand-in): a `stdbool.h` beside `main.hero` reads the library's and then
# defines `true` as 0, and the program's own folder is searched before the
# system's, so the runtime's `<stdbool.h>` would read it and `print(true)`
# print `false` at exit 0, measured with the refusal's call taken out. The
# guard gives back no `true` the unit takes from the library, so this case,
# unlike `special`'s two whose stand-in the reserved pair undoes, holds the
# class and not only the message. Refused at the program's first byte, the
# note naming the program's own folder; this line is its mark.

function main()
    b = true
    print(b)
